<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="color: #edf4fa;">Flywire is a proud sponsor of this year's "</span><em><a style="color: #223341;" href="https://www.nacubo.org/Publications/Advisories/AR-24-02-Best-Practices-for-Student-Financial-Responsibility-Agreements?utm_source=marketo&amp;utm_medium=email&amp;utm_campaign=q2clientnewsletter"><span style="color: #48b985;"><strong><u>Best Practices for Student Financial Responsibility Agreements: AR 24-02</u></strong></span></a></em><span style="color: #edf4fa;">" report published by NACUBO. </span></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><span style="color: #edf4fa;">A student financial responsibility agreement provides relevant information about official institutional policies to students and contractually binds them to those policies. Additionally, the agreement assists the institution and its collection agency partners when complying with laws and regulations.</span></p> </td> 
